Here is a warm, low-glare palette for a light theme. I kept the body text off pure black on purpose, since near-black text on a light page reads harsh and default.

:root {
  --bg: #faf8f4;
  --ink: #3a3630;          /* body text, a soft dark charcoal */
  --muted: #6f6a60;        /* secondary text */
  --accent: #2f6f8f;
}

Body text at #3a3630 on #faf8f4 still has plenty of contrast for reading, and the muted tone at #6f6a60 is fine for captions and timestamps. If you add an SVG chart, make sure the text fill inherits the ink token rather than falling back to black.
